+//    of each cell in linear light. The present path blends the new values into the previous light map with the
+//    time constant AMBIENT_TAU_S: the bars follow the picture within about 3 time constants, and a one-frame flash keeps
+//    only about a quarter of its strength.
+// 2. Bars: each bar pixel blurs the light map along the picture edge with a Gaussian. Farther from the picture,
+//    the blur is wider and the samples come from deeper in the picture.
+//    Light that is too bright is first compressed softly without a change of hue; then the brightness falls off
+//    with distance in linear light and reaches 0 smoothly at the screen edge.
+// 3. Seam: the part of the bar next to the picture (4% of the picture edge length, at most half the bar width) starts
+//    from the picture edge colour (the outermost light-map cell, strength 0.75, not compressed) and changes into the
+//    light, so the picture edge is no longer a hard step.
